---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How GICT collects, uses and protects personal information submitted through this website, admissions enquiries and corporate training requests."
  active="/privacy"
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 21 October 2026</p>
  <p>
    This policy explains how Global Institute of Corporate Training (GICT) handles personal information
    collected through this website. It applies to enquiries, admissions, campus visits and corporate
    training requests. It does not replace the terms in an admission offer or a signed contract.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact details you submit, such as name, email address and phone or WhatsApp number.</li>
    <li>The programme, mode, schedule, background and message you choose to share.</li>
    <li>Corporate enquiry details, such as company name, team size and training focus.</li>
    <li>Technical information normally processed by our hosting provider, such as IP address, browser type and pages requested.</li>
    <li>Consent records, including when and how consent was given.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your enquiry and provide the information you request.</li>
    <li>To assess programme fit and communicate about admissions, schedules and fees.</li>
    <li>To prepare a corporate training proposal where requested.</li>
    <li>To maintain records, prevent abuse and improve the website.</li>
    <li>To meet legal, tax and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Forms and WhatsApp</h2>
  <p>
    The enquiry forms on this website prepare a message and open WhatsApp so you can send it from your own
    account. The website itself does not store the form contents. Once you send a message through WhatsApp,
    WhatsApp and its parent company process the message under their own terms and privacy policies. If you
    prefer not to use WhatsApp, contact us by phone or email.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website is designed to work without advertising cookies. If analytics are enabled, we use them to
    understand aggregate traffic and improve content. Where required, analytics that use cookies will be
    loaded only after consent. The embedded map may set third-party cookies when it loads; you can use the
    “Open in Maps” link instead.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We may share information with service providers that help us operate the website, email, CRM, hosting or
    communications, and with professional advisers where necessary. We do not sell personal information. We
    may disclose information if required by law or to protect legal rights.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiry records are kept only as long as needed for the purpose for which they were collected, or as
    required by law. Retention periods may differ for admissions records, financial records and corporate
    proposals.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information. No website or
    messaging channel is completely secure. Please do not send sensitive documents through the website form
    or WhatsApp unless we have agreed a secure method.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask us to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, or withdraw
    consent to non-essential contact. Some records may need to be retained for legal or accounting reasons.
    Contact <a href="mailto:info@gict.edu.pk">info@gict.edu.pk</a> with your request.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The website is intended for adults and professional audiences. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children. If you believe a child has submitted information, contact us so we can remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the website or our processes change. The “last updated” date at the top of
    the page shows the current version.
  </p>

  <div class="prose-note">
    This policy is a general website notice. It should be reviewed with qualified counsel alongside GICT’s
    internal data-handling practices and any applicable Pakistani law.
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
